nCommunity\nStudent Life\nOverview\nStudent Awards\nFinancial Support\nStudent Clubs/Interest Groups\nSTUDENT SUPPORT AND WELLBEING\nSocial Good and Excellence\nCentre for Computing for Social Good and Philanthropy (CCSGP)\nCentre for Nurturing Computing Excellence (CENCE)\nOur Heritage\nNUS Computing Gallery\nResearch\nResearch\nOverview\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nResearch Partnership\nResearch Highlights\nKnowledge@Computing\nResearch Bulletin 2025\nResearch Prize\nNUS Computing Ascent Prize Awards\nEntrepreneurship\nInnovation and Entrepreneurship\nOverview\nLeadership\nInnovation\nFunding Opportunities\nAlumni Companies\nNews\nAwards & Competitions\nVenture Initiation Programme@NUSComputing\nNUS Computing Innovation Prize\nAsian Business Plan Competition\nThe Furnace\nOverview\nStart-ups\nIndustry\nIndustry Relations\nOverview\nIndustryConnect (iConnect)\nCareer Fair\nCareer Services\nInternships\nOverview\nFor Employers\nFor Students\nGiving\nNurturing Computing Talent\nMedals and Prizes\nSupporting Student Development\nBursaries and Financial Aid\nScholarships (Merit-based)\nProfessorships\nSpearheading Research\nSearch\nSearch\nMenu\nHome \u00bb Programmes \u00bb Graduate \u00bb PhD in Computer Science \u00bb Scholarships\nScholarships\nResearch Scholarships\nPresident\u2019s Graduate Fellowship (PGF)\nSingapore Digital (SG:D) Scholarship (Postgraduate)\nTuition Fees\nLoans\nMedical Insurance\nResearch Scholarships\nFinancial Assistance in the form of Research Scholarship is available, on a competitive-basis to all full-time students who meet the minimum criteria. The Research Scholarship will carry monthly emoluments, plus full tuition fee subsidy. Candidates with good undergraduate degrees in computer science, information systems or related disciplines are invited to apply for research scholarships. These are for pursuing full-time PhD programmes by research in the School. They are tenable for one year in the first instance and renewable annually for up to four years for PhD candidates, subject to satisfactory performance. Scholarship holders will receive a monthly allowance, and graduate students who passed their PhD Qualifying Examination will be awarded an additional top-up of S$500 per month (for two years) during their PhD candidature.\nThe details on the NUS Research Scholarships can be found here.\nPresident's Graduate Fellowship (PGF)\nThe PGF is awarded to candidates who show exceptional promise or accomplishment in research. A small number of PhD research candidates are selected each semester by the University for the Fellowship. The award is tenable for an initial one year and, subject to an annual review of the awardee\u2019s research progress, it can be renewable up to a maximum of 4 years.\nThe details on the PGF can be found here.\nSingapore Digital (SG Digital) Scholarship (Postgraduate)\nThe SG Digital Scholarship (Postgraduate) is an industry scholarship that empowers individuals interested in pursuing tech or media-related studies at the Masters or PhD level. Individuals pursuing postgraduate studies in specialised tech or media-related areas such as Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, Analytics, Immersive Media, and Digital Content Creation can chart their future with this scholarship.\nFind out more about the scholarship here.\nTuition Fees\nPlease refer to website at http://www.nus.edu.sg/registrar/administrative-policies-procedures/graduate/graduate-fees for the latest update.\nUnless otherwise indicated as one-time fee, mandatory miscellaneous fees as payable per annum.\nLoans\nStudents can request for loans up to 90% of their fees.\nMedical Insurance\nAll full-time candidates are required to enroll for the medical insurance scheme, unless they have already taken up similar insurance scheme themselves. Research scholars will be automatically enrolled in the medical insurance scheme, which will take effect from the first day of the following month after registration. The prevailing insurance premium will be deducted from the stipend on a monthly basis.\nClick here for PhD Online Application.\nResources for Current Students\nPhD in Computer Science\nDCS At A Glance\nWhy NUS Computer Science PhD?\nAdmission Requirements\nApplication Information\nIndustrial PhD Programme\nScholarships\nPhD Alumni\nGraduate Student Directory\nAwards\nOral Defense & Seminars\nEvents\nContact Us\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTelegram\nLinkedin\nYoutube\nSupport NUS Computing\nComputing 1\n13 Computing Drive\nSingapore 117417\n+65 6516 2727\nContact Us\nLocate Us\nFind Our Venues\nAdditional Links\nNUS COMPUTING\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nProgrammes\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nADMISSIONS\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nRESEARCH\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nDEPARTMENTS\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Information Systems and Analytics\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Information Systems and Analytics\nRESOURCES\nSchool Directory\nStudent Portal\nFacilities & Services\nNUS WebMail\nNUS Canvas\nStudent Jobs\nSchool Directory\nStudent Portal\nFacilities & Services\nNUS WebMail\nNUS Canvas\nStudent Jobs\nNUS COMPUTING\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nProgrammes\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nADMISSIONS\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nRESEARCH\nResearch Initiatives